  "heading": "X \\.mod./ R",
  "heading_latex": "X\\textrm{ mod }R\\quad\\htmlClass{mlg-title-written}{X / R}",
  "body_text": null,
  "page": null,
  "source": "[X \\.mod./ R]\nDefines: I := \\set@{ \\equivalence.class:of{x_}:over{R} : x_ \"in\" X }\nwhen:\n. X is \\set\n. R is \\equivalence.relation:on{X}\nDocumented:\n. called: \"$X?$ mod $R?$\"\n. written: \"X? / R?\"\n. description: \"The quotient set $X / R$ is the set whose elements are the\n                equivalence classes of $R$. It collapses each class to a single\n                point, so that elements related by $R$ become equal in the\n                quotient.\"\nId: \"cea0d898-a18d-44dc-b04c-ffb2f0cde26e\"",
